From: Slot RG353V build
Subject: [PATCH] wifi: rtw88: keep regulatory hardware writes on a running radio

Keep the regulatory state and adaptivity data current while the device is
stopped, but avoid SDIO transactions until normal channel configuration
reapplies transmit power after start. The existing device mutex serializes
this check with core stop/start. This fixes the captured regulatory disconnect
work versus mmc_sdio_resume host-claim deadlock.

---
--- a/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/regd.c
+++ b/drivers/net/wireless/realtek/rtw88/regd.c
@@ -487,7 +487,9 @@
 			  request->initiator);
 
 	rtw_phy_adaptivity_set_mode(rtwdev);
-	rtw_phy_set_tx_power_level(rtwdev, hal->current_channel);
+	/* Channel configuration reapplies power when the stopped radio starts. */
+	if (test_bit(RTW_FLAG_RUNNING, rtwdev->flags))
+		rtw_phy_set_tx_power_level(rtwdev, hal->current_channel);
 	mutex_unlock(&rtwdev->mutex);
 }
 
